(4) mixed-sign scaling solutions on lines carrying >=3 collinear source vectors
    rule: V = e^{-f.phi} V_perp(u); a local transverse minimum with V>0 exists for suitable |Lambda_i| iff the two
    extreme terms along the line are positive and a middle one negative (foot may lie outside: then the minimum is
    only local/metastable, V_perp -> 0+ beyond a barrier). Two-term (+,-): the critical point with V>0 is a maximum.
    flow direction = foot f; weak coupling & non-shrinking string-frame volume need f_rho>=0 and f_tau>=sqrt(3) f_rho
